## Symptom table

| If you observe | Check |
|----------------|-------|
| Unexpected exception | The raise site — Python's traceback names the file and line |
| Silent failure / wrong result | Return values and early returns in the entry points |
| Intermittent behavior | State held outside the function (globals, caches, env vars) |
| Slow execution | Loops, I/O, and any calls to other subsystems |

## Step-by-step diagnosis

1. **Reproduce the failure in isolation.**
   The first step for any {{ title | lower }} issue is a
   minimal reproduction. Strip the call down to its
   required arguments and confirm the failure still occurs
   outside the surrounding context.

2. **Enable verbose logging.**
{% if public_functions or public_classes %}
   If {{ title | lower }} logs anything, bump the level to
